{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And she covered her face.</b> She veiled her face, so that he would not recognize her." "<b>And she sat at the entrance of Enaim.</b> At the opening of the eyes — at a crossroads on the road to Timnah. And our Sages interpreted: at the opening of Abraham our father, toward whom all eyes look to see him (Sotah 10)." "<b>For she saw that Shelah had grown, etc.</b> Therefore she made herself available to Judah, for she longed to raise up children from him."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 38, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:02:36.561766204Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}